    {
      "_id": "byDTNTDbNnEDCkaH",
      "name": "Swallow",
      "type": "feat",
      "system": {
        "source": {
          "custom": "",
          "book": "MM'14",
          "page": "325",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
        "description": {
          "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p>The frog makes one bite attack against a Small or smaller target it is grappling. If the attack hits, the target is swallowed, and the grapple ends. The swallowed target is &amp;Reference[condition=blinded] and &amp;Reference[condition=restrained], it has &amp;Reference[rule=totalcover]{total cover} against attacks and other effects outside the frog, and it takes 5 ([[/damage 2d4 type=acid]]) damage at the start of each of the frog's turns. The frog can have only one target swallowed at a time. If the frog dies, a swallowed creature is no longer &amp;Reference[condition=restrained] by it and can escape from the corpse using 5 feet of movement, exiting &amp;Reference[condition=prone].</p></div>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "requirements": "",
        "uses": {
          "max": "",
          "recovery": [],
          "spent": 0
        },
        "type": {
          "value": "monster",
          "subtype": ""
        },
        "properties": [],
